WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.817
A bar chart is a natural display for a nominal variable.

00:00:03.817 --> 00:00:07.437
The bar lengths show counts, which are quantitative.

00:00:07.437 --> 00:00:11.607
The category labels themselves are not treated as measurements.

00:00:11.607 --> 00:00:16.507
We can reorder the categories by frequency or by a conventional order without implying that O minus A

00:00:16.507 --> 00:00:25.147
has any numerical meaning. This is a good example of matching a visualization to the measurement structure.

00:00:25.147 --> 00:00:31.362
The easiest way to classify a variable is to ask what statements are meaningful in the real world.

00:00:31.362 --> 00:00:36.422
Can values only be different, can they be ordered, are differences meaningful, and does zero mean absence?

00:00:36.422 --> 00:00:44.472
Those questions are more reliable than looking at whether the software stores the column as an integer or

00:00:44.472 --> 00:00:45.791
floating-point number.
